2186045417] [17592186554481 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554165 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554481 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554256 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554481 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554481 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554481 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186553997 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554481 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "790fc10f-cefb-5f65-a677-549fa2e80b47" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554492 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186553945 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554492 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554081 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554492 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554227 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554492 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554378 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554492 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554410 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554492 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554492 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554492 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186554378 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554492 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "98f4db4e-2c19-5da3-9efd-62ed734fe2e6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554547 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186554435 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554547 #edb/ref 1069 "q-134824" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554547 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554547 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/ae/ae6bc049d3bf3bbdf1a609b6cda4c3b4e9cc1699b387099d265e048a32be68d6.png)\n\nThe residual plot above was constructed after fitting a linear regression model on a set of bivariate numerical data $(x,y).$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. When $x=2,$ the regression equation overestimates the value of $y.$\n\nII. The residuals appear randomly scattered about the horizontal axis (there are no obvious trends).\n\nIII. This linear regression is probably a good fit for the data." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554547 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1f3c0f66-15fe-5ce9-aae2-49226c3a0199" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554547 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's examine the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The residual equals the actual value minus the estimated value:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \nFrom the plot, the residual at $x=2$ is positive. So, we have that $\\text{Actual}>\\text{Estimated},$ and therefore the model underestimates (*not* overestimates) this data point.\n\n- Statement II is false. The plot shows the residuals tend to decrease as $x$ increases. So, there is a trend, as shown below.\n\n![](images/2f/2f5f3a4dc75324a6ef415c987a62139e2dbd51c5b35a56d5a35f410781087c43.png)\n\n  \n\n- Statement III is false. Since the residuals are *not* randomly scattered above and below the horizontal axis, our regression line is *not* a good fit for the given data.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554549 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186554473 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554549 #edb/ref 1069 "q-134825" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554549 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554549 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/57/57ba7828008f3e3c271ae4c1b6d444005f40c09bf6ba99e614f3b6414c1e56c2.png)\n\nAn employee of a car dealership collects data on the value $y$ (in thousands of dollars) of a particular car model $t$ years after its release to the market. The residual plot above was constructed after fitting a linear regression model on this data set. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. When $t=6,$ the regression equation overestimates the value of $y.$\n\nII. The residuals appear randomly scattered about the horizontal axis (there are no obvious trends).\n\nIII. This linear regression is probably a good fit for the data." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554549 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "21d8d0de-cc80-527b-ade5-cff77e1f75ae" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554549 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's examine the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The residual equals the actual value minus the estimated value:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \nFrom the plot, the residual at $t=6$ is negative. So, we have that $\\text{Actual}<\\text{Estimated},$ and therefore the model overestimates this data point.\n\n- Statement II is false. The plot shows the residuals tend to decrease as time increases. So, there is a trend, as shown below.\n\n![](images/fe/fe18ccc94d0cc98f971b6482d4e31c7ec7066b5cec427108ddd8d1e6609e08ba.png)\n\n  \n\n- Statement III is false. Since the residuals are *not* randomly scattered above and below the horizontal axis, our regression line is *not* a good fit for the given data.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554579 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186554442 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554579 #edb/ref 1069 "q-134736" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554579 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554579 #edb/ref 1071 "A veterinarian collects data on a puppy's height $y$ (in inches) at certain times $x$ (in months) since it was born. The equation of the corresponding linear regression line for this data is \n\n$$\ny=2.2x+3.5.\n$$\n\nWhat is the residual after $5$ months if the actual height of the $5$-month old puppy is $15.5\\,in?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554579 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "66a5e8a2-f155-513a-b41f-dffb1f1fb098" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554579 #edb/ref 1074 "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute the estimated height using our linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{y} & =2.2x+3.5 \\\\  & =2.2(5)+3.5 \\\\  & =14.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =15.5-14.5 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is $1\\,in.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554595 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186554492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554595 #edb/ref 1069 "q-134788" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554595 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554595 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/f9/f940a05c937b3158ce737959dee4685d216e6d55d6651672aa910cdb2c492f1e.png)\n\nThe scatter plot for the data sets $x$ and $y$ of paired observations and the corresponding linear regression line are shown above.\n\nAccording to the regression model, what is the residual for the highlighted datapoint?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554595 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "855a07b7-e3c5-5f4d-b62e-d65fbbb7b6dd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554595 #edb/ref 1074 "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe highlighted datapoint has coordinates $(5,1).$ So, our actual value is $y=1.$\n\nOn the other hand, the point on the regression line that corresponds to $x=5$ has the $y$-coordinate $0.$ So, our estimated value of is $\\overset{^}{y}=0.$\n\n![](images/93/937c0307a74881c87e6a33c47b32a1ac2d5124326b13538455640cd9fc88c14e.png)\n\nTherefore, the residual is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =1-0 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554610 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186554477 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554610 #edb/ref 1069 "q-134719" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554610 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554610 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the data sets $x$ and $y$ of paired observations. The equation of the corresponding linear regression line for this data is \n\n$$\ny=-1.5x+2.\n$$\n\nAccording to the model, what is the residual at $x=12$ if the actual value of $y$ corresponding to this value of $x$ is $-14?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554610 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9d55db4e-8bf0-577f-a32c-7bdda150fe93" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554610 #edb/ref 1074 "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute the predicted value using our linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{y} & =-1.5x+2 \\\\  & =-1.5(12)+2 \\\\  & =-16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =-14-(-16) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554631 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186554481 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554631 #edb/ref 1069 "q-134753" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554631 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554631 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the data sets $x$ and $y$ of paired observations. The equation of the corresponding linear regression line for this data is \n\n$$\ny=1.8x+1.4.\n$$\n\nAccording to the model, what is the residual at $x=7$ if the actual value of $y$ corresponding to this value of $x$ is $12?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554631 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e8526d11-e962-5974-8b9d-23623deb26c8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554631 #edb/ref 1074 "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute the predicted value using our linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{y} & =1.8x+1.4 \\\\  & =1.8(7)+1.4 \\\\  & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =12-14 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554634 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186554439 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554634 #edb/ref 1069 "q-134830" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554634 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554634 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/31/31a72edb688af9be0481fc98346aa5655190e32564ddc003eb7bdd1c83d41ee1.png)\n\nAn economist records data on the volume of corn exports $y$ (in thousands of tons) from the United States to a particular country, $x$ number of years since $2010.$\nThe residual plot above was constructed after fitting a linear regression model on this data set. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. When $t=6,$ the regression equation underestimates the value of $y.$\n\nII. The residuals appear randomly scattered about the horizontal axis (there are no obvious trends).\n\nIII. This linear regression is probably a good fit for the data." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554634 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e996d8e3-bba2-534b-9d62-28bb3781b36f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554634 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's examine the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The residual equals the actual value minus the estimated value:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \nFrom the plot, the residual at $t=6$ is negative. So, we have that $\\text{Actual}<\\text{Estimated},$ and therefore the model overestimates (*not* underestimates) this data point.\n\n- Statement II is true. The plot shows that the residuals appear randomly scattered about the horizontal axis (there are no obvious trends).\n\n- Statement III is true. Since the residuals are close to $0$ and are randomly scattered above and below the horizontal axis, we can conclude that our regression line is probably a good fit for the given data.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554642 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186554448 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554642 #edb/ref 1069 "q-134737" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554642 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554642 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the data sets $x$ and $y$ of paired observations. The equation of the corresponding linear regression line for this data is \n\n$$\ny=0.75x+2.25.\n$$\n\nAccording to the model, what is the residual at $x=8$ if the actual value of $y$ corresponding to this value of $x$ is $11.25?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554642 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f64a4538-a38b-5427-b753-a3e4f5424a55" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554642 #edb/ref 1074 "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute the predicted value using our linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{y} & =0.75x+2.25 \\\\  & =0.75(8)+2.25 \\\\  & =8.25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =11.25-8.25 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554645 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186554447 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554645 #edb/ref 1069 "q-134797" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554645 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554645 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/81/815ba0a13bc8cbd7adcfadc63b80d6f2da36c9755166694915fa2f297be27721.png)\n\nAn employee of a car dealership collects data on the value $y$ (in thousands of dollars) of a particular car model $x$ years after its release to the market. The scatter plot for the data and the corresponding linear regression line are shown above.\n\nAccording to the regression model, what is the residual for the highlighted datapoint?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554645 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fd84baa2-dbd3-5523-aca7-04ab311e0400" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554645 #edb/ref 1074 "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe highlighted datapoint has coordinates $(6,12).$ So, our actual value is $y=12.$\n\nOn the other hand, the point on the regression line that corresponds to $x=6$ has the $y$-coordinate $10.$ So, our estimated value is $\\overset{^}{y}=10.$\n\n![](images/ab/ab5e194ac03482b1cee6bdb7aa35e323b40a1ad63769e60acbb000adb7aa1e82.png)\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =12-10 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is $$2\\,000.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
